d 'CODESCAN': module to scan wide-format code variables for pattern matches
d
d  codescan scans wide-format code variables, such as dx1-dx30 or
d proc1-proc20 in registry and claims data, for pattern matches
d using regular expressions or prefix matching, with rules given
d inline or read from a reusable CSV or Stata code dictionary. It
d creates binary indicators or per-row counts for each defined
d condition, supports exclusion patterns, applies lookback and
d lookforward time windows around a reference date, reports
d prevalence, and can collapse to patient-level summaries or merge
d them back onto the rows. Results are returned in r() and can be
d placed in a named frame, saved as a dataset, or exported to CSV
d or Excel. Diagnostics include per-variable contributions,
d pairwise co-occurrence, and multi-window sensitivity with
d denominators. The companion command codescan_describe inventories
d the code values in the same variables before any rules are
d written and can draft a starter codefile. It works with ICD, KVA,
d CPT, ATC, OPCS, or any string code system. 
d
d KW: ICD codes
d KW: diagnosis codes
d KW: procedure codes
d KW: drug codes
d KW: registry data
d KW: claims data
d KW: pattern matching
d KW: regular expressions
d KW: comorbidity
d KW: code lists
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
f codescan.ado
f ../_/_codescan_engine.ado
f ../_/_codescan_codefile.ado
f ../_/_codescan_definitions.ado
f ../_/_codescan_outputs.ado
f ../_/_codescan_parse_filespec.ado
f ../_/_codescan_validate_path.ado
f ../_/_codescan_tostring.ado
f codescan.sthlp
f codescan_describe.ado
f codescan_describe.sthlp
